<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	What the app declares for a sandboxed (Mac App Store) build, which Phase 1 does not
	ship: the sandbox itself is not switched on, and the ad hoc signature here carries no
	hardened runtime. When it is, the loopback servers need network.server, the app's own
	calls to them need network.client, and the bundled Node runs JIT-compiled code so it
	needs the two memory entitlements. No other entitlement is requested: the app does not
	use the camera, microphone, contacts or location.

	Bluetooth (Phase 4): com.apple.security.device.bluetooth is the App Sandbox entitlement for
	CoreBluetooth. It does nothing for this ad hoc, unsandboxed build, where the permission
	prompt is driven by NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription in Info.plist; it is declared now so
	the sandboxed build does not have to remember it. (From Apple's documentation; not yet
	exercised with a sandboxed build.)
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.bluetooth</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
